class:: HenonMap
summary:: Trigger-driven raw Hénon map coordinates
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/HenonSonify, Classes/GbmanMap

description::

Iterates Michel Hénon's 1976 two-dimensional map: code::x' = 1 - a*x*x + y:: and code::y' = b*x::. Both next coordinates use the old state. A rising trigger advances once; reset restores the supplied initial coordinates, and non-finite recurrence state also restores them.

The outputs are raw state coordinates. They are not normalized audio signals and may diverge for some parameters.

Like link::Classes/Stepper::, HenonMap holds between trigger edges; unlike Stepper, its next value comes from a coupled nonlinear recurrence and both coordinates are exposed.

subsection:: State-space portrait

image::henon-map-phase.png#The default Hénon attractor after a 2,000-iteration transient. x is horizontal and y is vertical; each coordinate is fitted independently to use the frame clearly.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on each nonpositive-to-positive edge. Audio or control rate.
argument:: a
Quadratic coefficient, sampled at the event; not clipped.
argument:: b
Old-x coupling coefficient, sampled at the event; not clipped.
argument:: x0
Initial x coordinate, sampled at construction and reset.
argument:: y0
Initial y coordinate, sampled at construction and reset.
argument:: reset
Restore initial state on a rising edge.
Returns:: Two audio-rate outputs: x and y.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments and two outputs.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ HenonMap.ar(Impulse.ar(100))[0] * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(HenonMap.kr(Impulse.kr(12))[0].linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 80, 2000), 0, 0.1) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Real-time phase portrait

The same coordinates drive the sound and the bounded on-screen trail. Close the window to free the synth.

code::
(
SDPhaseView.open(
    "Hénon map: x-y phase portrait",
    [-1.5, 1.5], [-0.5, 0.5],
    { HenonMap.kr(Impulse.kr(90)) },
    { |state|
        Pan2.ar(
            SinOsc.ar(state[0].clip(-1.5, 1.5).linexp(-1.5, 1.5, 100, 1800), 0, 0.06),
            state[1].clip(-0.5, 0.5).linlin(-0.5, 0.5, -1, 1)
        )
    }
);
)
::

